\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Coarse gauge fields and effective weights}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{Replacing a chain of links by its ordered transport retains
a group element between its endpoints. Two retained paths may
share links, and retaining the same path twice produces equal
variables. Which measure on these retained transports reproduces
the fine observables, and how does it respect changes of vertex
frames?}

\p{The fine law may use the [compact gauge transfer
weights](fdip-007Y), or any integrable gauge-invariant weight.
The [holonomy convention](fdip-006F) fixes the order of path
products. Haar coordinates, conditional integration and the
[Gauss average](fdip-00L4) describe the retained law. The final
comparison asks whether convolving two SU(2) Wilson weights
can be represented by changing a single coupling.}

